<decision #track.flow_dsl_reference.owner apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" } (
  <question ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2D>
  Where is Flow DSL reference content authored and versioned?
  </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2D>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2E>
    Use depa-flows canonical docs/flow-dsl as the only authored source.
    </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2E>
    <decision-text ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2F>
    Only in depa-flows canonical docs/flow-dsl; the package module is a generated projection.
    </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2F>
    <rationale ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2G>
    This prevents Eidolon and Halfcode from maintaining divergent copies of depa-owned semantics.
    </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2G>
    <evidence ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2H>
    The 29 canonical Markdown files and their byte identities are frozen by the package generator and focused tests.
    </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2H>
  )>
)>

<decision #track.flow_dsl_reference.shape apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" } (
  <question ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2J>
  Is the published unit another system Skill?
  </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2J>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2K>
    Publish a shared authoring module, not another installed system Skill.
    </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2K>
    <decision-text ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2M>
    No. It is a shared Halfcode authoring module with WikiPage resources that downstream Skills consume through explicit ResourceMappings and no sibling Skill dependency.
    </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2M>
    <rationale ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2N>
    The installed product surface remains four system Skills while reusable reference knowledge stays composable.
    </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2N>
    <evidence ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2P>
    The generated ResourcePackage contains WikiPage resources and no SkillCapsule resource.
    </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2P>
  )>
)>

<decision #track.flow_dsl_reference.public_entry apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" } (
  <question ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2Q>
  Where is the loader exported?
  </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2Q>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2R>
    Export the loader from an isolated package root.
    </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2R>
    <decision-text ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2S>
    From the isolated ai-workflow-flow-dsl-reference package root.
    </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2S>
    <rationale ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2T>
    Documentation assets and package location remain independent of AI workflow runtime and browser graphs.
    </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2T>
    <evidence ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2V>
    The package has one compiled root export and only an exact Halfcode runtime dependency.
    </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2V>
  )>
)>

<decision #track.flow_dsl_reference.release apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" } (
  <question ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2W>
  Which package version changes and how is the registry selected?
  </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2W>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2X>
    Start at 0.1.0 and use the user's active npm configuration.
    </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2X>
    <decision-text ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2Y>
    The new package starts at 0.1.0 with exact Halfcode 0.2.3; npm uses the user active configuration with no registry override.
    </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2Y>
    <rationale ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2Z>
    This is the terminal smallest patch and preserves the user's registry authority.
    </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M2Z>
    <evidence ?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M30>
    Package metadata, lockfile, pack validation, and the release procedure contain no registry override.
    </?01M0NJZ4PTDBX59S5JD27A6M30>
  )>
)>
